^SERIES = GSE78234
!Series_title = The HDAC inhibitor Panobinostat (LBH589) exerts in vivo anti-leukaemic activity against in MLL-rearranged Acute Lymphoblastic Leukaemia and involves the RNF20/RNF40/WAC – H2B ubiquitination axis
!Series_geo_accession = GSE78234
!Series_status = Public on Jul 12 2017
!Series_submission_date = Feb 23 2016
!Series_last_update_date = Mar 25 2019
!Series_pubmed_id = 28690313
!Series_summary = We demonstrate the in vivo efficacy of the histone deacetylase inhibitor Panobinostat (LHB589) against MLL-rearranged ALL using xenograft mouse models of MLL-rearranged ALL cell lines and primary patient cells. Panobinostat monotherapy showed strong anti-leukaemic effects, extending survival and reducing overall disease burden. Comprehensive molecular analyses in vitro showed the anti-leukaemic activity in MLL-rearranged ALL to involve depletion of H2B ubiquitination via suppression of the RNF20/RNF40/WAC E3 ligase complex.
!Series_overall_design = Gene expression was measured using  Affymetrix platform in 4 distinct cell lines treated or untreated in vitro with Panobinostat  at 5 nM for 24 hours. Four independent biological replicates were carried out.
!Series_type = Expression profiling by array
!Series_contributor = Luca,,Trentin
